{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Prints the whole SONG chain of a TT-303PATGEN instance (all cells, with their repeats) as one real MIDI item, so a finished arrangement of the eight slots becomes a fixed track. Turn on SEQ LINK in TT-303PATGEN first, select the target track, put the edit cursor where the item should start and run the script. It asks how many times the chain is printed in a row (1 = one pass). Slides are written as overlapping notes, ties as longer notes, accent and normal velocities as set in the plug-in (same rules as "TT-303PATGEN Print to MIDI Item", which must be installed next to this script). PROB and HUMANIZE are not printed.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Prints the pattern of a TT-303PATGEN instance as a real MIDI item, so the live generator becomes a fixed track. Turn on SEQ LINK in TT-303PATGEN first (the script reads the pattern from the gmem namespace tt303pg), select the target track, put the edit cursor where the item should start, run the script and enter the number of bars. Slide is written as overlapping notes, ties as longer notes, accent and normal velocities as set in the plug-in. PROB and HUMANIZE are not printed (the item contains the pattern as written).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-303PATGEN\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI-only acid pattern generator for REAPER. Generates 303-style patterns (16 to 32 steps, note / octave / gate / tie / accent / slide / probability per step) and plays them as MIDI, synced to the host transport. Accent = velocity above the synth's threshold (default 127 vs. 64, threshold 65 as in the TT-303 1.5.0), slide = overlapping legato notes - exactly what the TT-303 expects in HOST mode, and what any other mono synth understands. Five algorithms (random walk, Markov, Euclid, motif+variation, classic mutation), ten scales plus a custom mask, seeded and reproducible, mutate / rotate / reverse / invert / double, eight pattern slots (A-H), song chain, 32 built-in style patterns plus 16 factory scenes, swing, humanize, MIDI transpose (C2 = original pitch) and an optional gmem link (namespace tt303pg). Operated from the drawn front panel; all parameters stay automatable.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TT-303 ACID MACHINE \u8212- mono acid synth in the style of the TB-303. Tribute, no samples, no sample ROM, all model.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CONTROLS AS ON THE ORIGINAL TUNING semitones (-24..+24), plus FINE in cents SLIDE glide time between tied notes, 0..300 ms CUTOFF filter frequency, ~150 Hz .. ~2 kHz exponential (rises with resonance) RESONANCE feedback of the 18 dB ladder up to self-oscillation ENV MOD depth of the filter envelope, up to 5.2 octaves DECAY decay of the filter envelope, ~30 ms .. ~570 ms ACCENT level AND filter boost of the accent circuit WAVEFORM sawtooth / square\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODEL DETAILS (after R. Whittle / Devil Fish documentation)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Filter: 3-pole ladder (18 dB/oct) in ZDF/TPT form, level-dependent feedback k/(1+0.4|y|), 2x oversampled, then 3-point decimation. Soft clip only at the master, never in the OS loop (it never engages there at real levels anyway).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Pole correction 1/(1+0.10*kRes): mild peak correction; the resonance hump moves up with rising resonance, as on the reference.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Feedback HP 20 Hz IN the feedback path (DC block).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Square with frequency-dependent duty + tilt, classic 1-sample PolyBLEP.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Accent capacitor: recharge +0.95, saturation 1.65. Accent sweep with non-linearity and slight cutoff dependency.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab On accent: fixed 0.2 s filter decay + shortened VCA attack (1.8 ms).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Slide: constant time, log frequency space; the same note stays held.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FX: delay/reverb bypassed at mix < 0.5 %. EQ OFF = true bypass.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI: notes are consumed, CC/pitchbend keep going.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPERATING MODES HOST Pure sound generator, played from the piano roll. Velocity >= threshold = accent, overlapping notes = slide. The same note again while held is ignored (Devil Fish: the first note-off ends it). Last note wins from a stack of 10 held notes (the oldest falls out); CC 64 (sustain) keeps the gate on while its value is >= 64 (Devil Fish). Accent threshold default 65; the DF button steps through the Devil Fish thresholds 65 / 80 / 100 / 120. SEQ Internal 16-step sequencer, four pattern banks A-D with copy function, random and mutation, shuffle, gate length. Runs on the project timeline or free (FREE RUN). MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch). MIDI OUT also sends the sequence out. All four banks travel with the project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Effect path: ahead of each of the three units \u8212- WaveShaper (Soft/Hard/ Fold/Fuzz), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb \u8212- sits an input EQ as a dual slider (lowcut left, highcut right, 0..20 kHz). After that compressor (-14 dB, 5:1) and master.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The input EQ only shapes what is sent into each effect; the dry signal runs alongside untouched. On the drive what the EQ removes is added back after the WaveShaper, so a raised lowcut takes the bass out of the DISTORTION, not out of the output (drive off = transparent).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPTIONS box: FONT SIZE (FONT 1/2) and a custom HSV colour picker (FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG) with RESET / RESET ALL, live and per instance, with low-contrast warning; TOOLTIPS ON / OFF (saved with the project), tooltips on every control.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A slide into the same note ties (no retrigger, one note-on at SEQ OUT); pattern and bank edits create a REAPER undo point and UNDO restores the bank it was made in; the mouse wheel steps whole-number knobs one step at a time.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 PRESETS: bar in the header, left of OPTIONS: [<] [name v] [>] [SAVE] [...]. FACTORY = INIT, TT-Groove, TT-BigBoy, TT-HiImTom!, TT-OffbeatBaby, TT-GoodStart (the default presets of the web version, each with its sound and the four pattern banks A-D); USER = 32 slots that travel with the project (@serialize, after the four pattern banks; old projects load with an empty bank). A user preset holds all sound sliders (2..20, 27..32, 34, 35), the pattern settings (length, shuffle, gate, active bank 21/22/23/25) AND the four pattern banks A-D. Not part of it: MODE, FREE RUN, SEQ OUT, MIDI THRU, UI Color, transport. A native REAPER preset file of this plugin carries the whole bank.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI: THRU at the top of the header passes INCOMING notes on to the output (CC and pitchbend always pass through anyway). SEQ OUT in the sequencer panel sends the SELF-GENERATED sequence out. Two different sources, hence two switches. In SEQ mode incoming notes are transpose commands \u8212- whoever also passes them on with THRU sends them out next to the sequence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 SURFACE after the Tim Techlor design kit: Core Black, Core White, Acid Green #39FF14, traces at a 45 degree angle with solder pads. Wordmark in Zilap Orion, if installed. Labels sans-serif (Segoe UI / Helvetica Neue / DejaVu Sans / Arial), numeric values monospaced (Consolas / DejaVu Sans Mono / Menlo / Courier New). Which of these is present the script measures itself. The front computes in a fixed design grid and scales to the window size \u8212- to enlarge, just drag the FX window open. HiDPI is honoured via gfx_ext_retina. All internal JSFX sliders are hidden ("-" before the name), operation is exclusively via the device front.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-BPM2MS2HZ\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Converts note values at the project tempo into milliseconds and Hertz, in a tool window drawn in the TimTechlor UI kit look (ReaImGui).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The tempo follows the project by default; the slider switches to a manual tempo, FROM PROJECT switches back to sync.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Click any value to copy it to the clipboard.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tabs: NOTE VALUES (1/1 to 1/32, dotted, triplets) and BARS (1 to 64 bars, selectable time signature).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab OPTIONS: tooltips on/off, AUTO FIT, UI size, font size, dotted and triplet rows, wordmark watermark. All settings are saved.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Manual: bpm2ms2hz-manual.html next to the script.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires the ReaPack extension "ReaImGui: ReaScript binding for Dear ImGui" (cfillion, repository "ReaTeam Extensions").\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-THEMEFONTEDITOR\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Find and change the font sizes of the active REAPER theme.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Picker: hover over any text in the REAPER window, click or press Shift to lock it. The editor shows which WALTER font (or ini font) is used there.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Change size, bold and italic; element overrides give single WALTER elements a font of their own.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Changes are previewed live through a working copy; "Bake theme" writes a new theme {\f1 <Name> (TimTechlor)} (original untouched) or, if chosen under BAKE TO, back into the original (previous version kept as .bak).\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires ReaImGui (0.10+) and js_ReaScriptAPI (both in ReaTeam Extensions). Manual: TT_ThemeFontEditor_Manual.html next to the script.\par}
}
